35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found that seventy percent of costs are fixed, and a third of renewals needed reminders. We need a structure that accounts for this reality.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, the data confirms my fear. People hesitate because the commitment feels too large. We need to lower that barrier.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, the data is brutal. The same nine people do the heavy lifting, while eighteen never show up. We need to fix this imbalance.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, the ledger confirms the fixed costs. But the hours are the real shock. Chasing individual payments takes six hours monthly, versus one for yearly.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, this is why the quiet ones drift. They fear a huge yearly bill. We need a way to let them ease in without feeling lost.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, six hours chasing payments is unsustainable. We need a system that reduces that admin burden, not just a flat fee.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Toshio, that administrative load explains the friction. If we simplify the payment cycle, we might reduce the hesitation people feel about committing.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Toshio, that admin load is a symptom, not the cause. The real problem is that nine people carry the weight while eighteen pay and vanish.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the admin load is the cause of the burnout. If the treasurer quits, the fee structure collapses. We must prioritize sustainability.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I hear you, but if the quiet ones leave, the club shrinks. We need a fee that welcomes them in gently, not one that pushes them away.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, I agree, but we can't ignore the cash flow. If we offer easy entry, we need a clear path to full commitment so the books stay balanced.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, exactly. A gentle entry point that still leads to stability. We need to make belonging feel safe, not like a trap.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Kenji, I get it, but ""gently"" doesn't fix the fact that the same nine are drowning. We need to see who is actually carrying the load before we talk about easing anyone in.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the load is heavy, but the structure determines the weight. I need to see if the fixed costs can be spread more evenly to protect the next treasurer.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I agree. Spreading the cost helps, but the real barrier is the fear of a big upfront bill. We need a way to start small.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,I am worried about setting a figure by guesswork. We need a structure that balances the fixed costs with the reality of who actually pays on time.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. The hesitation stems from fear of a large, opaque commitment. We need a structure that feels safe and transparent, so people can belong without anxiety.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"I am done guessing. The data proves the imbalance. We need a structure that forces participation, not just payment.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I am done guessing. The data proves the admin burden is unsustainable. We need a structure that protects the treasurer from burnout, not just the members from fear.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I am done guessing. The data proves the fear is real. We need a structure that lets newcomers start small, so they stay and eventually commit.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
